Subject: [PATCH 45/55] Drone tracks: Shift + Kit makes a held kit row a drone
 row; a row without a lane at its own pitch; a new track's row selected; the
 arpeggiator in a row's menu

Fixes and gaps found reviewing the previous two commits against the plan, checked in the emulator (tests/song,
run.sh's DRONE=1: drone_rec_emu.py presses the pads and buttons as the user does, InstrumentClipView::padAction()
and Buttons::buttonAction()):

- Making a kit row a drone row never worked: the previous commit put the Kit button's new case (a row's audition pad
  held, or an empty row's pad held to add one) after the two cases that already take Kit with a pad held (the row's
  sample browser, the drum creator), so it was never reached. Now it is Shift + Kit, checked ahead of them; Kit alone
  opens the sample browser as it always has. In the emulator: a gate row and a row being added made drone rows, each
  sounding its 200 Hz while its pad is held, at the drone's level (+0.02 dB), the clip view staying, and saved as
  droneTone rows.
- DroneDrum::noteOn(): a row without an Hz lane starts at its tone's own pitch. The drum's lane offset is one for all
  clips of the kit, so after a clip whose lane had moved the pitch, a note in another clip of the kit (a new one made
  in Song view, say) kept that offset.
- SessionView::createNewDroneTrack(): the first row whose tone is on (else the first row) is the new kit's selected
  row. A new kit has none, and the clip view's select encoder then changes the kit instead of turning a row's pitch.
- droneTrackToneMenu: the arpeggiator and randomizer submenus, as a gate row's menu has them; before, only the sound
  editor's shortcut pads reached a drone row's arpeggiator.

Checked: tests/drone 150 checks passed (renderTone() bit for bit the drone's tone); tests/song demand run
(EMU_OPTS="--init-sounds --seed 1") measured.wav 87a7df29 as v14/v15; DRONE=1 all checks passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
